1
00:00:06,710 --> 00:00:09,200
A coin lands heads five times in a row.

2
00:00:09,250 --> 00:00:13,390
A friend says: tails is due next, it is more likely now!

3
00:00:13,440 --> 00:00:15,040
Is tails more likely now?

4
00:00:15,090 --> 00:00:20,330
Pause the video and choose: no, it is still a half, or yes.

5
00:00:20,380 --> 00:00:20,540
No.

6
00:00:20,590 --> 00:00:22,130
The coin has no memory.

7
00:00:22,180 --> 00:00:25,520
The probability of tails is still a half.

8
00:00:25,570 --> 00:00:30,310
Remember: for a fair coin, the probability of a head is a half.

9
00:00:30,360 --> 00:00:36,360
Two events are independent if one happening does not change the probability of the other.

10
00:00:36,410 --> 00:00:41,320
Two spins of a spinner, or two tosses of a coin, are independent.

11
00:00:41,370 --> 00:00:45,930
Believing that tails is due is called the gambler's fallacy.

12
00:00:45,980 --> 00:00:46,630
Your turn.

13
00:00:46,680 --> 00:00:50,650
Taking a counter and putting it back before the next pick.

14
00:00:50,700 --> 00:00:54,250
Does that make the events independent, or dependent?

15
00:00:54,300 --> 00:00:57,520
Pause the video and choose.

16
00:00:57,570 --> 00:00:58,380
Independent.

17
00:00:58,430 --> 00:01:02,450
With replacement, the bag is the same every time.

18
00:01:02,500 --> 00:01:05,870
Events are dependent if one affects the other.

19
00:01:05,920 --> 00:01:08,620
A bag has 10 balls, numbered 1 to 10.

20
00:01:08,670 --> 00:01:11,370
Take one out, and do not put it back.

21
00:01:11,420 --> 00:01:13,480
Now 9 balls are left.

22
00:01:13,530 --> 00:01:17,610
If the first ball was odd, 5 even balls are left out of 9.

23
00:01:17,660 --> 00:01:21,360
So the chance the second is even is 5 ninths.

24
00:01:21,410 --> 00:01:22,040
Your turn.

25
00:01:22,090 --> 00:01:28,090
If the first ball was even, and not replaced, what is the probability the second is even?

26
00:01:28,140 --> 00:01:29,170
Give a fraction.

27
00:01:29,220 --> 00:01:32,070
Pause and work it out.

28
00:01:32,120 --> 00:01:34,510
4 even balls are left, out of 9.

29
00:01:34,560 --> 00:01:37,190
The probability is 4 ninths.

30
00:01:37,240 --> 00:01:38,520
Here is the method.

31
00:01:38,570 --> 00:01:43,160
Step 1: does the first result change what can happen next?

32
00:01:43,210 --> 00:01:46,610
Step 2: with replacement: independent.

33
00:01:46,660 --> 00:01:49,490
Step 3: without replacement: dependent.

34
00:01:49,540 --> 00:01:51,590
Recount what is left.

35
00:01:51,640 --> 00:01:57,600
Step 4: in real life, think about whether one event really affects the other.

36
00:01:57,650 --> 00:02:00,180
A bag has 3 red and 7 blue counters.

37
00:02:00,230 --> 00:02:03,120
The first is red, and it is not replaced.

38
00:02:03,170 --> 00:02:04,910
2 red are left, out of 9.

39
00:02:04,960 --> 00:02:08,400
The chance the second is red is 2 ninths.

40
00:02:08,450 --> 00:02:15,200
It rains today, and it rains tomorrow: probably dependent, because weather comes in spells.

41
00:02:15,250 --> 00:02:17,640
A fair dice gave three 2s in a row.

42
00:02:17,690 --> 00:02:20,990
The chance of a 2 next is still 1 sixth.

43
00:02:21,040 --> 00:02:24,010
A roulette wheel has landed on red 6 times.

44
00:02:24,060 --> 00:02:26,270
Jack thinks about the next spin.

45
00:02:26,320 --> 00:02:28,220
Which line is wrong?

46
00:02:28,270 --> 00:02:29,410
Line 1 is wrong.

47
00:02:29,460 --> 00:02:31,890
The spins are independent.

48
00:02:31,940 --> 00:02:35,330
The probability of black has not changed.

49
00:02:35,380 --> 00:02:44,270
Casinos make money partly because players believe in the gambler's fallacy, and keep betting on the result that seems due.

50
00:02:44,320 --> 00:02:45,510
One last question.

51
00:02:45,560 --> 00:02:48,670
Roll a 6 on a dice, and toss a head on a coin.

52
00:02:48,720 --> 00:02:50,460
Independent, or dependent?

53
00:02:50,510 --> 00:02:53,720
Pause the video and choose.

54
00:02:53,770 --> 00:02:54,570
Independent.

55
00:02:54,620 --> 00:02:57,390
The dice cannot affect the coin.

56
00:02:57,440 --> 00:03:02,110
To remember: independent means one does not affect the other.

57
00:03:02,160 --> 00:03:04,840
With replacement: independent.

58
00:03:04,890 --> 00:03:07,640
Without replacement: dependent.

59
00:03:07,690 --> 00:03:10,190
Coins and dice have no memory.

60
00:03:10,240 --> 00:03:15,630
Great work! Now practise lesson 12.2 on Camday.
